      "label": "Where does a page's lock property live? (coherence)",
      "excerpt": "Where does a page's lock property live? (coherence)",
      "text": "is <spell-page> written in spell or TS?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T13:41:52.326Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T13:42:21.129Z",
          "html": "<p>TypeScript, by hand (<code>Page.ts</code>, <code>page.py</code>).  Only <code>two sided view</code> and <code>notebook</code> are written in spell, generated into both cores.  Q8 A makes a page half spell (a generated base, <code>start()</code> by hand);  B keeps it all TypeScript.  More in Q8.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T13:42:08.456Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "q8",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Where does a page's lock property live? (coherence)",
      "excerpt": "Where does a page's lock property live? (coherence)",
      "text": "Would it be better for <spell-page> to be a base class like View?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T13:43:54.042Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T13:44:39.126Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes, I now recommend B:  <code>Page</code> is a base class like <code>View</code> and <code>App</code>, all hand-written TypeScript with a Python twin;  spell-written templates are types built on them.  <code>lock</code> becomes one more hand-written member, and <code>Notebook.spell</code> goes with nothing replacing it.  More in Q8.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T13:44:15.018Z"
      }
    }
  },
